```python
import re

def extract_assert_statements(code):
    pattern = r"// @@@\s*(.*)"
    matches = re.findall(pattern, code, re.MULTILINE)

    for i, match in enumerate(matches):
        print(f'<code>Debug.Assert({match});</code>')

# Test the function
extract_assert_statements("""
// @@@ Value of x increases by y in the function
// @@@ first index of x in the list remains same if x was already a value in the list
""")
```

This program uses Python's regular expressions (`re`) to match any comment starting with `// @@@`. The following line of code extracts comments that start with `// @@@` from the provided C# source code and outputs them in the `<code>` block as a valid Assert statement.

